Z||000003||Nashco||11-21-2001||10:27 AM||||I have been wanting to install a remote start unit.  I do have a 5 speed (holds wrist out to be slapped) but I don't park on any hills and I do use my e-brake anyway.  I live up in Michigan during the coldest months of the year, so it really sucks warming up your car.  If the unit was affordable, I'd be interested...I'm on a tight budget right now, so if I can't afford it I could always bookmark this thread and save it for later.<P>So, what units are you guys using?  What'd it cost you?  What do you think of it?  What are its features?<P>Thanks in advance <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||11-21-2001||10:40 AM||||Well, the one in my Bravada was a gift from my in-laws.  It came from Audio King and was professionally installed there. (probably around $150 at the time).<P>The one for my Fiero (not yet installed) I picked up off Ebay for around $80.  They can now be gotten there in the $50 range  ( <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597886269&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=597886269&r=0&t=0</A>  ) You just have to install it yourself!||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||11-21-2001||02:13 PM||||I have one called "Auto Start" installed by my cousin in Fargo ND.  I love it.  Here in Colorado they arn't as common as in the colder areas so it is cool to start it in the parking lots and seeing people look.  Best feature is the remote door locks followed by remote trunk release.||||reg||1
