Z||000010||rogergarrison||11-21-2001||06:31 PM||||picture hitting the button in your house and forgeting you were drunk last nite and left it in gear. now run out the door barefoot and chase your car down the block.....almost catching it......but not before it ran into a neighbors house and thru the wall.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula||11-21-2001||07:07 PM||||how does it push the cluthc in to start it.  And if it did start in gear wouldnt it just stall?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Nashco||11-21-2001||07:32 PM||||Yeah, if you had it in gear, the chances of getting it to actually start are slim; BUT, with a cheaper unsophisticated unit, it may keep on trying until the battery finally died or the car chugged into something.<P>The system doesn't push the clutch in, you have to bypass the clutch switch so that it is always acting as if the clutch pedal is in.  So, clutch says it's in, you leave it in neutral, and hit the starter.  Technology rules! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||11-21-2001||07:37 PM||||As long as you keep it in neutral, you'll be fine.  It's that one time you parked right up to you're new car, left it and gear, and realize it a split second after you pressed the button.  You'll get to watch it lurch forward into the other car- I'm sure you'll never do it again!<P>BTW: Mine is installed on an Automatic vehicle, so this is not experience talking.  But I will admit to getting in and reactivating the starter... that's not a nice noise.||||reg||1
Z||000014||grinthock||11-21-2001||10:11 PM||||MinnGreen --  Most starters have anti-grind.  Mine won't fire if it see's more than 12V present, if there is more than 12V then the car MUST be running.||||reg||1
Z||000015||artherd||11-21-2001||10:26 PM||||When I do mine, there will be both an optical, and electro-mechanical, 'in-gear' seonsor on the tranny itself. (not the shifter, cables could break  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000016||84fierotrevor||11-21-2001||10:28 PM||||Will a remote starter work on my 84 fiero ?<BR>cuss I heard myiron duke doesn't really have fuel injection, It has some sorta "kinda" fuel injection ||||reg||1
Z||000017||CoolBlue87GT||11-21-2001||10:30 PM||||I have a remote start I installed in my Ford Contour.<P>Made by DesignTech, called AutoCommand. I got it at Target, for around 65 dollars.<P>Took about 4 hours to hook up.<P>It does have many safety features built in.<P>1. A hood switch, when the hood is open, the remote is disabled.  - So you don't get your fingers chewed up while under the hood.<P>2. On a automatic, if the brake is pressed, or put in gear, the engine is stopped (when the key is not in the ignition)<P>3. For a manual transmation, uses the  neutral safety switch circit, won't allow engine to be started unless in neutral.<P>- The clutch switch is bypassed only when the neutral switch tells the remote starter its in neutral when attempting to start.<P>4. After started, will run for ten min, then shut off.<P>5. Has a hidden switch inside, that allows you to exit the car, taking the key with you.<BR>- Same rules apply, will shut off if brake is pushed, hood is raised, or ten min goes by. <P>6. Same switch can disable remote starter if wanted.<P>7. Can be used with alarm systems, with a universal alarm bypass module.<p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000018||FieroMaster88||11-22-2001||01:14 AM||||As soon as I get my power locks and install them and fix my E-Brake I will have keyless entry and remote start.  My alarm also does remote "trunk" release, and that is hooked up now.  Just need to get the keyless entry and remote start hooked up before it gets really cold!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
